  "remaining_limits": [
    "One 24-case run per adapter on native macOS ARM64, plus one 22-case old-keeper baseline. No fuzz corpus, random mutation campaign, reliability estimate or other native platform qualification.",
    "These probes address the keeper inside the guest and the shared codec. They do not qualify the VMM host vsock multiplexer, host administrative parser, broader forbidden-egress or shared-cache matrices.",
    "Closed payload schemas and connection-owned controls are not authentication or general replay prevention; there is no new global instance/session selection API.",
    "Known valid headers can still declare up to 16 MiB and wait for incomplete bodies. Per-connection read deadlines, connection/thread admission, aggregate memory and denial-of-service behavior remain unqualified.",
    "Per-read probe timeouts are diagnostics for these fixed fixtures; reported header-refusal observations are not a universal latency bound.",
    "The minimal guests have no Nix/service/agent/editor workload. Earlier density, preparation, stop-receipt, CLI/TLS and trusted Remote-SSH rows retain their original keeper hashes and are not transferred to this new keeper.",
    "The Rust suite reuses the exact shared keeper files and experimental SSH server. One existing OpenSSH test remains ignored by default; the root project full integration suite and Linux confinement rows were not rerun here.",
    "New private disks/controller directories are removed after owned helper/endpoint cleanup. Compiler cache pruning preserves runtime executables and evidence; it does not establish a full 8-GiB environment storage pass."
